*** SYNCHRO 2 *** : attends que le Groupe B ait fini B-04 'Contrôle LED'.

Crée driver_station.py :

  import socket
  sock = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_DGRAM)
  sock.bind(('0.0.0.0', 4210))
  sock.settimeout(0.5)
  ROBOT_IP = '127.0.0.1'  # changer pour IP ESP32
  PORT = 4210
  while True:
      print('1-LED ON  2-LED OFF  3-PING  4-Capteur  q-Quitter')
      c = input('Choix : ')
      if c == '1': sock.sendto('LED_ON'.encode(), (ROBOT_IP, PORT))
      elif c == '2': sock.sendto('LED_OFF'.encode(), (ROBOT_IP, PORT))
      elif c == '3':
          sock.sendto('PING'.encode(), (ROBOT_IP, PORT))
          try: r,_=sock.recvfrom(1024); print('Reponse:', r.decode())
          except: print('Pas de reponse')
      elif c == '4':
          sock.sendto('GET_SENSOR'.encode(), (ROBOT_IP, PORT))
          try: r,_=sock.recvfrom(1024); print('Capteur:', r.decode())
          except: print('Pas de reponse')
      elif c == 'q': break

settimeout(0.5) evite de bloquer si le robot ne repond pas. Le try/except attrape le timeout.
